vkd3d-proton: sampler feedback on two 32-bit planes, tier from R32 atomics

Sampler feedback maps (DXGI_FORMAT_SAMPLER_FEEDBACK_*) were R32G32_UINT images
written through R64_UINT atomics, and Tier 0.9 required shaderInt64 and
shaderImageInt64Atomics -- both unavailable on Metal/MoltenVK.  With
dxil-spirv 0200 the map is two interleaved R32_UINT planes:

  - utils.c: both feedback formats map to VK_FORMAT_R32_UINT (4 bytes) and
    their UAV/compatibility view format is R32_UINT; device.c creates the
    feedback UAV as R32_UINT.
  - vkd3d_private.h: d3d12_resource_desc_get_padded_feedback_extent() returns
    twice the padded width (texel 2x = mips 0-7, 2x + 1 = mips 8-14 + encoded
    MinMip); image creation, CopyResource and the feedback UAV clear all use
    it, so they cover both planes.
  - command.c: encode/decode views are R32_UINT.
  - shaders: decode fetches the two texels of the requested plane with
    texelFetch -- exactly the texels and clamping the upstream textureGather()
    with a nearest CLAMP_TO_EDGE sampler at an integer corner returned -- and
    reads the encoded MinMip from plane 1; encode loads/stores both planes.
  - device.c: Tier 0.9 now requires what the lowering and resolve shaders use:
    R32_UINT optimal storage-image atomics and sampling, a 2D (array) R32_UINT
    image of 2 * (16384 / 4 + 16) texels and 2048 layers, demote/helper
    invocation and fragment stores.  FL 12_2 still needs VRS tier 2 etc.
  - cache.c: shader revision 2, so no cached R64 feedback SPIR-V survives.

Verified on the host (Apple M1 Max, MoltenVK 1.4.2, argument buffers on) with
a native macOS build of this tree: the upstream d3d12_sampler_feedback tests
and a CPU-reference test for mips 8-14 (tests/gpu/sampler-feedback).

